      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the adult person from <Video 1>. Keep identity as in <Video 1>: the same face, hair, body proportions, and presence. Render in HD realistic live-action style: photoreal skin texture, real camera look, not anime, not 2D, not illustration. Change only the outfit: replace whatever they wear in <Video 1> with the target clothing described in the shot (clean wardrobe edit). Do not change body shape, face, or identity.\n<Subject 2> is the background environment from <Video 1>. Keep the same place, lighting, and setting as in <Video 1>, rendered HD realistic.\n<Video 1> is the sole visual reference. Preserve composition, camera, framing, pose, motion timing, <Subject 1> identity, and <Subject 2> from <Video 1>. Edit clothing only: apply the new outfit on <Subject 1>; keep fabric motion natural and consistent with pose. Output style is HD realistic photorealism only. Do not invent anime style labels or extra character features beyond identity, background, the clothing change, and HD realistic look.\n<Audio 1> is the original music track provided. Keep the exact same music: same melody, arrangement, mix, tempo, and timing. Do not remix, replace, duck, mute, or restyle the music. There is no separate voice reference; do not invent or replace a sung/spoken voice track.\nsummary:\n[reference generation + video reference + audio reference] HD realistic photorealism. Follow <Video 1> only for picture. Maintain the same person and the same background. Change clothing/outfit only; keep identity, camera, pose, and motion from <Video 1>. Continuous single shot matching <Video 1> timing. Not anime, not 2D. Keep <Audio 1> music unchanged.\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout [Shot 1]): attribute_transfer - same character identity from <Video 1>; clothing/outfit replaced with the target wardrobe; style kept HD realistic photorealism.\n<Subject 2> (appears throughout [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - same background from <Video 1>